# Chakra UI agent rules (helenhaircut)

This project uses **Chakra UI v3** (`@chakra-ui/react`). Prefer current v3 APIs; do not invent v2 patterns.

Official AI surface (all three): https://chakra-ui.com/docs/get-started/ai/mcp-server · https://chakra-ui.com/docs/get-started/ai/llms · https://chakra-ui.com/docs/get-started/ai/skills

## 1. MCP (live lookup — prefer this)

Configured in `.cursor/mcp.json` as `chakra-ui`:

```bash
npx -y @chakra-ui/react-mcp
```

Use MCP tools before guessing:

- `list_components` / `get_component_props` / `get_component_example`
- `get_theme` / `theme_customization`
- `v2_to_v3_code_review` when touching old v2 code

Optional Pro templates need `CHAKRA_PRO_API_KEY` in MCP `env` (do not invent a key).

If Cursor does not detect the server, restart or enable **MCP Tools → chakra-ui**.

## 2. LLMs.txt (docs context fallback)

When MCP is unavailable, attach Chakra docs via Cursor `@Docs`:

- `https://chakra-ui.com/llms.txt` — index
- `https://chakra-ui.com/llms-full.txt` — full v3 docs
- Scoped: `llms-components.txt`, `llms-styling.txt`, `llms-theming.txt`
- Migration: `llms-v3-migration.txt`

Prefer MCP over pasting full docs into context.

## 3. AI Skills (installed — follow when relevant)

Installed under `.agents/skills/` via official:

```bash
npx skills add https://github.com/chakra-ui/chakra-ui/tree/main/skills
```

| Skill | Use when |
|-------|----------|
| `chakra-ui-builder` | Build/create UI, theming, charts, setup |
| `chakra-ui-migrate` | v2 → v3 upgrades / breaking changes |
| `chakra-ui-refactor` | Review or convert existing UI to v3 Chakra |

Skills activate from natural language (no need to name them). They default to v3 and check `package.json`. Read the matching skill’s `SKILL.md` before substantial Chakra work.

## Suggested agent flow

1. For build/migrate/refactor intents → load the matching Chakra skill.
2. For props/examples/tokens → query Chakra MCP.
3. If MCP is down → `@Docs` with the smallest relevant `llms-*.txt`.
4. Implement with v3 compound components and semantic tokens; keep Astro island rules (hydrate only when interactive).

## Project conventions

- Chakra is the only UI kit for section components.
- Interactive islands wrap with client `Provider` (`src/components/ui/provider.tsx` / islands).
- Prefer semantic tokens and Chakra layout primitives over ad hoc CSS.
